# Pinned HRX (amdxdna) release consumed by the HRX runtime path.
#
# SOURCE: the public FastFlow SDK (ROCm/FastFlow-SDK) GitHub releases. HRX is
# supplied as a prebuilt release asset downloaded + verified + extracted by
# fetch-hrx-release.{sh,ps1}; there is NO dependency on any private HRX fork and
# nothing is built from source. FLM consumes the extracted package via
# find_package(hrx CONFIG REQUIRED) / hrx.mk under ./.hrx-release/.
#
# NOTE (draft branch): the FastFlow SDK release asset pinned below ships the HRX
# *runtime* (libhrx.so) but does NOT yet bundle the HRX dev package (public
# headers + lib/cmake/hrx). Until a FastFlow SDK release publishes the HRX dev
# package, fetch-hrx-release.sh will download+verify this asset but then report
# that no HRX CMake package config was found, and the engine build cannot link.
# When such a release is available, bump TAG/ASSET/SHA256 below (and the Windows
# pair) -- no other change is needed.
HRX_RELEASE_REPO="ROCm/FastFlow-SDK"
HRX_RELEASE_TAG="fastflow-sdk-v0.1.0.dev202610050001"
# For Linux.
HRX_RELEASE_ASSET="fastflow-sdk-linux-x86_64.tar.zst"
HRX_RELEASE_SHA256="009ff6da889e83ec444a01c7deb62974bba93314ba0fe97c9546b01b508b32f0"
# For Windows.
HRX_RELEASE_ASSET_WINDOWS="fastflow-sdk-windows-x86_64.zip"
HRX_RELEASE_SHA256_WINDOWS="2f6a42c1e973ac1cb24241eaf1fef15f9e0d5d66b193ed5d81ea23493393b633"
